{
  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's perception and motion capabilities, separating sensing (uncontrollable events) from motion (controllable events). The specification automaton encodes safe, coverage-oriented exploration: in clear states, the robot moves forward or random_walks; on obstacle detection, it enters a dedicated recovery state with a single corrective action, then returns to exploration as soon as the path is clear. move_backward is used only for front-obstacle recovery, never chained, and never in clear/search states. full_rotate is reserved for repeated blockages. All transitions are deterministic and respect the event and state constraints.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for perception and motion, with all events as specified.",
    "Specification automaton encodes safe, progress-oriented exploration with conservative recovery, rapid return to exploration, and strict avoidance of unsafe actions in obstacle states."
